.TH VALIDATE-INTAKE-GOVERNANCE-CONFIG 1 "2026-09-13" "0.2.2"
.SH NAME
validate-intake-governance-config \- validate language-aware requirements governance
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B validate-intake-governance-config.sh
.BI --config " FILE"
.RI [ --repo " PATH" ]
.RI [ --json ]
.PP
.B validate-intake-governance-config.sh
.BI --journal " FILE"
.RI [ --json ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Validates schema 2.0 documentation language, naming profiles, portable roles,
collection paths, legacy aliases, and migration journals without modifying the
repository.
.SH OUTCOMES
Configured collections report Aligned, MigrationRequired, NeedsClarification,
or Blocked. Eligibility is an ordering result and grants no delivery authority.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero means Aligned or a valid journal. One means migration or clarification is
required. Two means blocked or invalid input.
.SH LIFECYCLE
Completed members must be archived. Non-completed members must be active.
Completed series retain their archived members with no eligible candidate.
SeriesManifest accepts an absent empty active directory; DirectoryStrict does not.
activeIntakeCount counts physical matching active files; activeSeriesTargetCount
counts active series members. RIG017 reports lifecycle mismatches, without writes.

.SH PHYSICAL PATH BOUNDARIES
Collection roots must resolve to distinct locations inside the repository. Active
targets cannot resolve into the archive. Unknown series and target states return
RIG017; aliased roots return RIG007 and repository escapes return RIG004.
